<Base title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <img class="portrait" src="/headshot.png" alt="James Coppock" width="160" height="160" />
  <p class="lede">I'm James, an applied scientist and ML leader. I take AI from research to production in high-stakes healthcare, where the answer has to be right and you have to be able to show why.</p>
  <p>At Infinia ML, the AI arm of revenue-cycle company Aspirion, I lead the ContractIQ and Pricing & Scoring teams. I've shaped ContractIQ from its earliest design through to production. It turns complex payer contracts into structured, auditable reimbursement logic, so providers can see exactly what they should be paid and catch underpayments. Pricing & Scoring uses ML to find the denied and underpaid claims most worth appealing. Across both, my job is setting technical direction and building a team that brings real rigor to revenue integrity.</p>
  <p>The thread runs back further than healthcare finance. I started with signals from motion: sensors inside footballs at Wilson, then heart rate and cuffless blood pressure from wearables at Valencell. My PhD at Duke moved inside the body, building deep-learning methods for MRI that measure how spinal discs respond to load. At Bionic Health (now Thrive Wellness), I led Data Science & AI, building pipelines that combined imaging, health records and wearable data into disease-risk predictions and decision support for clinicians.</p>
  <p>I live in Durham, North Carolina, with my wife, in a century home we've been <a href="/life/restoration">restoring</a>. Off the clock I'm <a href="/life/training">training</a>, taking <a href="/life/photography">photos</a>, or in section 113 for a <a href="/life/hockey">Canes game</a>.</p>
</Base>
